---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout title="Nanovision | Coverage Reports">
    <main class="pt-24 pb-16 min-h-screen bg-background">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
            <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6">Coverage Reports</h1>
            <p class="text-xl text-muted-foreground mb-8">
                Nanovision supports various coverage report formats as input.
            </p>

            <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
                <h3>Supported Formats</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Cobertura XML</strong>: A standard format used by many tools (Java, Python, etc.)</li>
                    <li>
                        <strong>Go Cover Profile</strong>: The native format for Go coverage (<code
                            >go test -coverprofile</code
                        >)
                    </li>
                    <li><strong>LCOV / GCov</strong>: Common in C/C++ and other environments.</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>How it works</h3>
                <p>
                    Nanovision parses these reports to understand which lines of code have been executed during your
                    tests. It normalizes this data into a common internal representation to generate unified reports.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>
</Layout>
